                "word": "ogee",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6c6efbf5-642b-42e1-af0b-f1a3bafff172",
                        "entry_id": "3323a5cf-43c6-3fd0-82a8-9ae9890c72a5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ogees"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39eb179f-63d5-32e5-a94a-f51b35190d7a",
                        "entry_id": "3323a5cf-43c6-3fd0-82a8-9ae9890c72a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A double curve in the shape of an elongated S; an object of that shape."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb2f2747-18a2-4f7d-98b1-11a44fdb8ca8",
                                "sense_id": "39eb179f-63d5-32e5-a94a-f51b35190d7a",
                                "text": "At the centre of this façade of one story is a porch of two stories with a tall attic and a gable of ogee outline flanked by finials."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "64361471-2353-45e2-aaa5-44142eb5cddc",
                                "sense_id": "39eb179f-63d5-32e5-a94a-f51b35190d7a",
                                "text": "There is no pronounced ogee arch anywhere, though there is a suspicion of one where the open trefoils of the gables rest upon the containing arches. The tracery too of all the circles is geometrical, i.e., composed of simple curves; there is no flowing or ogee tracery with compound curves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22379ac1-c4a2-4ad3-9c15-d38a6b12ed4a",
                                "sense_id": "39eb179f-63d5-32e5-a94a-f51b35190d7a",
                                "text": "In front of the leading splasher the frame was given what is called an ogee bend outwards, [...]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f95fe8c-14c8-3a8a-b281-6da9e9c337a0",
                        "entry_id": "3323a5cf-43c6-3fd0-82a8-9ae9890c72a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A pointed arch made from two ogees."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0a42115-c90c-3cdd-a42d-3eae982c36ba",
                        "entry_id": "3323a5cf-43c6-3fd0-82a8-9ae9890c72a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An inflection point."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "497fad40-eb72-3af5-9c63-15c24ac11a6c",
                        "entry_id": "3323a5cf-43c6-3fd0-82a8-9ae9890c72a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The malar or cheekbone prominence transitioning into the mid-cheek hollow."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
